{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2420,"output":5629,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3933,"totalTokens":8049,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Let me analyze each item.\n\nQ021: source: \"which you do not understand: ...\" target: \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解：...\" — target adds \"即使你懂得这种语言\" (even if you understand this language), source says \"which you do not understand\" (you do NOT understand). Direction flipped: source asserts you don't understand it; target says even if you understand it. Also target omits \"which you do not understand\" meaning. FINDING, claim_type CONDITION or DIRECTION. target_span: \"即使你懂得这种语言\". Correction: \"这是你无法理解的语言\" or similar. Evidence: \"which you do not understand\".\n\nQ022: \"You cannot stop us now!\" → \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" fine. \"watched silently as the races fought and burnt the land\" — \"他默默注视着各个种族争战不休，将大地付之一炬\" fine. \"remake it, only better\" → \"将它重塑得更加美好\" ok. \"summon Him through\" ok. No issues.\n\nQ023: \"A slot in the door opens and a pair of wild eyes peer out.\" → \"门上开了一个小洞，一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他。\" \"peer out\" means looking out from the slot; \"凝视着他\" — \"he\" whom? The player. Source doesn't specify \"him\" but \"凝视着他\" — the player asking is \"你\". Referent issue: target says 眼睛凝视着他 but source says eyes peer out (looking outward). \"凝视着他\" — adding \"他\" - who is 他? The player would be \"你\" in next line. Hmm, ADDITION/REFERENT. This is a common MTEnglish style. It's a plausible addition; could be UNCERTAIN or FINDING. Actually \"peer out\" = 向外张望, whereas 凝视着他 implies staring at him. I'd say FINDING on \"凝视着他\" — evidence \"peer out\". Actually it's arguably minor. Given the next line addresses the player as 你, \"他\" is inconsistent referent. I'll mark FINDING with REFERENT: correction \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外张望\" or \"打量着外面\". Hmm, but rule 3: new info compatible with evidence isn't a defect. \"凝视着他\" introduces a third person referent not present. I'll mark as FINDING, claim_type REFERENT.\n\nAlso \"A slot in the door opens\" — 小洞 vs slot (缝隙/投信口). \"开了一个小洞\" — a slot opens. Minor, acceptable.\n\nQ024: fine.\n\nQ025: \"orbs of command\" → \"指令水晶球\" — orb = 球, crystal added. In ToME \"Orb of Command\" is 指令宝球? Adding 水晶 — \"crystal\" not in source. But rule 3: additions compatible... hmm, 水晶 is specific new info (crystal) — orb could be crystal, so compatible? Orb of Command in game is a crystal ball? It's a quest item that's an orb. Adding \"水晶\" specifies material — can't be judged wrong by visible evidence. Probably fine. \"in my travels\" omitted — \"我没能找到所有的指令水晶球\" — \"in my travels\" omitted, minor. \"请问我可以让你们的人来帮我寻找\" fine. OMISSION of \"in my travels\" is trivial; probably not report.\n\nQ026: fine.\n\nQ027: \"Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" → \"几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" Tense: source future \"I'll have everything prepared\"; target past/completed \"准备好了\" — Chinese 了 can be future perfect too. \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — could read as future. Minor. \"which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago\" → \"那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方\" — fine, \"men of Sholtar\" → 肖尔塔人. \"return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" → \"请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率\" — fine. \"It opens the ruins of Telmur\" → \"它可以打开泰尔玛废墟\" ok. Acceptable.\n\nActually \"Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared\" — conditional: if you return in a few days, I will have everything prepared. Target \"几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — okay-ish. Not report.\n\nQ028: \"you are called to serve\" → \"你效力的时候到了\" ok. \"the nearby unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless\" → \"附近不洁沼泽中的居民正在蠢蠢欲动\" ok. \"find the source\" → \"找到这一切的源头\" — \"这一切的\" addition, compatible. Fine.\n\nQ029: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" → \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙。\" — \"Nothing but hatchlings\" means we've only encountered hatchlings (nothing except hatchlings). Target says \"从未遇上幼龙\" = never encountered hatchlings. DIRECTION/VALUE flipped! FINDING. Evidence: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far.\" Correction: \"到目前为止只遇到幼龙\". claim_type: VALUE or DIRECTION. I'll use VALUE (only vs never). Actually DIRECTION works too. \"Nothing but X\" = only X. Target negates. FINDING.\n\nAlso \"Cover a dragon\" — \"我们得到的龙皮连一条龙都盖不住\" fine. \"spared no expense\" → \"不惜血本\" fine. \"dwarven Thronesmen\" → \"钢铁王座\" fine. \"wyrmic\" → \"龙战士\" fine. \"turn her draconic talents to FINDING some dragons\" → \"把操控龙族力量的本事用来找出几条龙\" — \"draconic talents\" → 操控龙族力量的本事, fine-ish. \"Now, if only she could...\" → \"现在只盼她能...\" fine.\n\nQ030: \"Report for bad behavior\" → \"举报我的不良行为\" — \"my\" added. Source is a label for reporting someone's bad behavior; \"我的\" — in context, reporting the player's behavior? Could be reporting yourself? \"举报我的不良行为\" means \"report MY bad behavior\" which is odd — usually you report someone else's. Actually this might be a UI to report your own bad behavior (e.g., to get penalty)? Hmm. Without context, \"my\" is added info. This is ToME's Lua chat \"Report for bad behavior\" — probably reporting a player. Adding \"我的\" changes the object. UNCERTAIN or FINDING. Evidence \"Report for bad behavior\". I'd say FINDING with SUBJECT/ADDITION: target adds \"我的\". Correction: \"举报不良行为\". Hmm, but could the context be self-report? ToME chat has a command to report bad behavior... Actually in ToME there's a chat option where players can report griefers. \"我的\" seems wrong. But rule 3: additions compatible with evidence and not judgeable wrong — can we judge \"我的\" wrong? The report is for bad behavior; whose? Ambiguous. I'll mark UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ031: \"Place the object where?\" → \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" — \"Place\" vs \"丢弃\" (discard/throw away). Placing ≠ discarding. FINDING, ACTION. Evidence: \"Place the object where?\" Correction: \"将物品放到哪里？\"\n\nQ032: \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\" → \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币。\" — target adds \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中\" — achievement name addition. Source is achievement desc text; adding the achievement name... The source likely is the achievement description \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces\" which is the achievement itself. Adding \"在...成就中\" — is it judgeable wrong? The source itself is the achievement description; saying \"在成就中积累\" is meta. Rule 3: new info compatible and not judgeable wrong — but is it? The source describes the action done by the player; \"在成就中积累3000金币\" suggests accumulating gold within the achievement, which is a bit off but... Hmm. In ToME, this achievement is \"Gold Rush\"? Actually \"Greedy dragon\"? Hmm — the achievement for 3000 gold in ToME is \"Greed\" or similar. \"龙之贪婪\" (Dragon's greed) — I can't verify externally. Rule 1 says no external knowledge. The addition of the achievement name can't be judged wrong by visible evidence? Actually it could be: the source is the achievement's own description; translating it as \"in the X achievement, accumulate 3000 gold\" is consistent with a list of achievements. Not clearly wrong. I'd not report, or report UNCERTAIN. Hmm. The phrasing \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币\" — as an achievement description this is a common localization pattern. I'll skip or UNCERTAIN. Let me be careful; I'll skip it (empty candidates) since it's plausibly correct formatting. Actually \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces\" — target matches core meaning. Skip.\n\nQ033: fine.\n\nQ034: \"I will not let you down!\" → \"我一定会让你失望的！\" — opposite meaning! \"not let you down\" = 不会让你失望. Target says \"一定会让你失望\" (will definitely disappoint you). FINDING, DIRECTION. Evidence: \"I will not let you down!\"\n\nQ035: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" → \"竞技场生存至第20轮。\" — 50 vs 20! FINDING, VALUE. Evidence: \"Got to wave 50\".\n\nQ036: \"Now, this is impressive!\" → \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\" — \"这个发现\" (this discovery) added. Source: \"this is impressive\" referring to something. Adding \"发现\" — context unknown; could be judged? \"this\" could be anything. The addition specifies it's a discovery — can't be judged wrong from visible evidence. Rule 3 — skip. Hmm, but could be a slight SCOPE narrowing. I'd skip.\n\nQ037: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\" → \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\" — \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" → \"野心并获得永恒的生命\" — power omitted? \"野心\" = ambitions (wild dreams), \"power\" omitted. Actually \"成就你的野心\" covers \"wild dreams\" but \"of power\" omitted, and \"eternal life\" is in the \"获得永恒的生命\" part. So \"power\" is omitted. OMISSION, minor. \"成就你对力量与永恒生命的狂野梦想\" would be full. Is omission of \"power\" substantive? It's a real omission. I could report FINDING OMISSION: target_span \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命\", evidence \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\". Hmm, modest but objective. I'll report it as FINDING? It's arguably substantive (power dropped). Given rules, omission of \"power\" is objective. I'll include, maybe as FINDING. Or UNCERTAIN since 野心 vaguely implies power-lust. I'll go FINDING with OMISSION... Actually the meaning is fairly retained (ambition for power is implied by lich). I'll mark UNCERTAIN? Hmm. Let me decide: \"wild dreams of power and eternal life\" — target: \"野心\" (ambition) + \"永恒的生命\". Power dropped. It's an objective omission but low severity. I'll report FINDING with claim_type OMISSION.\n\nQ038: \"Kickin' it old-school\" → \"现代风格\" (modern style) — opposite! FINDING, DIRECTION. Evidence: \"old-school\". Correction: \"老派风格\" / \"复古怀旧\".\n\nQ039: \"Killed a boss while already dead.\" → \"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\" — fine (that's the actual ToME achievement \"While you're dead\" — you kill a boss while dead i.e., as undead? Actually source: killed a boss while already dead). Target matches. Fine.\n\nQ040: \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" → \"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\" — \"in orbit\" (在轨道上) vs \"在地面上\" (on the ground) — opposite! FINDING, VALUE/DIRECTION. Evidence: \"maintain it in orbit\". Correction: \"使其稳定在轨道上\". Also \"Abashed Expanse\" → \"次元浮岛\" — name translation differs, but can't judge externally; the orbit/ground flip is judgeable. FINDING.\n\nNow Q023 reconsider: \"peer out\" → \"凝视着他\". The slot opens and eyes peer out — outward. \"凝视着他\" (staring at him) — direction and referent. Who is \"他\"? The doorkeeper addresses the player as 你. So 他 has no referent. I'll report FINDING, claim_type REFERENT: target_span \"凝视着他\", evidence \"peer out\". Correction: \"一双狂乱的眼睛向外张望\".\n\nQ021: source \"which you do not understand\" — this is a fragment from a longer text (ToME: \"in a tongue which you do not understand\"). Target: \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\" — flips to \"even if you understand this language, you cannot understand\". Wait — actually there could be context: \"you hear words in a language which you do not understand\". Target's rendering changes meaning. FINDING, CONDITION/DIRECTION. target_span \"即使你懂得这种语言\". evidence \"which you do not understand\". claim_type: CONDITION. Correction: \"这是你无法理解的语言\" or \"你听不懂这种语言\".\n\nQ030: decide. \"Report for bad behavior\" — I'll report UNCERTAIN with ADDITION of \"我的\". Actually hmm — in ToME, there's a \"Report bad behavior\" in chat to report other players. \"举报我的不良行为\" would mean \"report my bad behavior\" — that's clearly odd. But without external knowledge, whose behavior? The phrase \"Report for bad behavior\" lacks possessive. Adding \"我的\" — could the source be a button for a player to report themselves? Unlikely but unknowable. I'll go UNCERTAIN, ADDITION.\n\nQ032: skip or UNCERTAIN? The achievement name \"龙之贪婪\" (Dragon's Greed) — actually in ToME there's achievement \"Greed\" for 3000 gold... can't verify. Rule 3 allows additions compatible. Skip — empty candidates? But schema requires items array with 20 items; candidates can be empty. Observation still needed. I'll give Q032 empty candidates with observation.\n\nHmm wait, but maybe the target's \"在...成就中\" — the source \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\" is itself the achievement description; rendering as \"在X成就中积累3000金币\" is a standard style. Skip.\n\nQ036: \"Now, this is impressive!\" → \"这个发现\" — the addition \"发现\". Could be judged? If the speaker is reacting to something shown, \"this\" may not be a discovery. ToME: this line... unknown. Rule 3: can't judge wrong. Skip. Or UNCERTAIN ADDITION. I'll skip. Hmm, actually I'll include UNCERTAIN ADDITION since \"这个发现\" narrows \"this\" to a discovery, unsupported by source. Borderline. Rule 4: UNCERTAIN only when evidence points to problem but real ambiguity. The addition is unsupported but might be contextually right. I'll include UNCERTAIN, ADDITION. Hmm, that might be over-reporting. Actually rule 3 explicitly says additions compatible with evidence and not judgeable wrong are not defects. \"this is impressive\" — \"this\" being a discovery is compatible. Skip. Empty candidates.\n\nQ037: include FINDING OMISSION for \"power\". Actually let me reconsider: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\" Target: \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\" \"野心\" translates \"wild dreams\" roughly. \"of power\" omitted. Yes, report. FINDING? The omission is objective: \"power\" has no counterpart. Severity low but objective. Verdict FINDING.\n\nHmm, \"成就你的野心\" —野心 already connotes desire for power somewhat in Chinese. But \"power\" explicit word dropped. I'll report as FINDING OMISSION... or UNCERTAIN. I'll say FINDING since it's directly verifiable omission of a content word. Correction: \"成就你对力量与永恒生命的狂野梦想\".\n\nQ025: \"in my travels\" omitted — trivial adverbial. Skip. Also \"orbs of command\" → \"指令水晶球\": \"水晶\" addition — crystal orb, compatible. Skip.\n\nQ027: \"I'll have everything prepared\" → \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — \"肯定\" addition, fine. Skip.\n\nQ028: skip.\n\nQ022: check \"He who felt great sorrow\" — 他为这个世界深感悲痛 ok. \"You cannot stop us now!\" ok. Skip.\n\nQ024: empty.\n\nQ026: empty.\n\nQ033: empty.\n\nQ039: empty.\n\nNow write observations for each item (min length 1). Output JSON with all 20 items in order.\n\nCandidates per item:\n- Q021: FINDING CONDITION\n- Q022: []\n- Q023: FINDING REFERENT\n- Q024: []\n- Q025: []\n- Q026: []\n- Q027: []\n- Q028: []\n- Q029: FINDING VALUE (\"Nothing but hatchlings\" vs \"从未遇上幼龙\")\n- Q030: UNCERTAIN ADDITION\n- Q031: FINDING ACTION\n- Q032: []\n- Q033: []\n- Q034: FINDING DIRECTION\n- Q035: FINDING VALUE\n- Q036: []\n- Q037: FINDING OMISSION\n- Q038: FINDING DIRECTION\n- Q039: []\n- Q040: FINDING VALUE (orbit vs ground)\n\nWrite JSON."}}
